{
  "_comment": "Family mapping rules. Each family has: name (display), layer (DXF layer suffix - the actual layer becomes <layer>_BOUNDARY), color (AutoCAD ACI color 1-255), and keywords. Keywords are matched WHOLE-WORD and case-insensitively, not as bare substrings: plain containment put 'FRESH AIR ATTENUATORS' into the TEN family and '8M EXPRESS WAY' into PRESS. Order matters - the first family with a match wins, so put the more specific families first, and inside a family put longer keywords before the short ones they contain. Anything matching nothing lands in 'Unknown' (UNKNOWN_BOUNDARY layer, color 7). Edit this file, restart the app, and re-run Section 3 / Section 4. Extending it also improves label choice, because a text the family rules recognise is treated as a room name rather than an equipment tag.",
